        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18-a2">

                <pb facs="0345" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv08/pg335"/>

                <head>Appendix B to HD–59</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-19"><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 19,
                            1919</date>.<lb/>Received: September 20, 1919.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Translation</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: Sir G. Clerk, Bucharest.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: Supreme Council, Paris.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bratiano, much excited by the story of the children’s hospital, asks me to
                    inform the Conference that he has received from Budapest a report proving that
                    the doctors directing the children’s hospital in this city have declared in
                    writing that neither the Rumanian authorities nor any Rumanian subject in this
                    hospital has taken away any medicine, dressings, or other sanitary objects, and
                    that consequently the children’s lives have not been endangered. The military
                    authorities at Budapest have requested the inter-Allied Commission to
                    investigate this affair.</p>
            </div>
